<title>USA: Thermo Electron to buy back units' shares.</title>
<headline>Thermo Electron to buy back units' shares.</headline>
<dateline>WALTHAM, Mass. 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thermo Electron Corp on Monday said its board authorized the repurchase of up to $50 million of the securities of its publicly held subsidiaries through December 20, 1997.</p>
<p>The company said the authorization is in addition to a separate buyback authorization for about $21 million, which expires September 1997.</p>
<p>Thermo Electron said it spent about $105 million in 1996 to repurchase securities under previous authorizations.  </p>
<p>The company's publicly traded subsidiaries include Thermedics Inc, Thermo Cardiosystems Inc, Thermo Voltek Corp, Thermo Instrument Systems, ThermoSpectra Corp, Thermo Sentron Inc, ThermoQuest Corp, Thermo Terratech Inc, Thermo Remediation Inc, Thermo Power Inc, ThermoTrex Corp, Thermolase Corp, Thermo Ecotek Corp and Thermo Fibertek Inc.</p>
